  "body": "Found by the read-only second review of PR #2927. The finding comes from a read of the code. No run proves it.\n\n## What can happen\n\nA STEP file can use the short entity names of ISO 10303-21. The short name of `PLANE_ANGLE_UNIT` is `PLANUN` (public ISO short-name registry, `https://standards.iso.org/iso/10303/tech/short_names/short-names.txt`, line 1554). The solidcore p21 parser does not map this name, and PR #2927 does not add it.\n\nA file that states its angle unit as degrees with the short name then has no angle unit that the reader can find. The reader uses radians. An angle that the file gives in degrees, for example the semi-angle of a cone, is then read as radians. The surface has the wrong shape, and no refusal or note tells the user.\n\nWrong geometry is wrong output for each toolpath and each gouge check. Thus the priority is `P1` until a test shows the correct angle or a refusal.\n\n## Where\n\n- `crates/kernel/src/solidcore_step.rs`: the rename step that PR #2927 adds for `GUAC` and `SUNT`, and the unit read after it.\n- The same registry gives `GC` for `GLOBAL_UNCERTAINTY_ASSIGNED_CONTEXT`. It is not mapped. That changes the tolerance only: check it in the same work.\n\n## What is expected\n\n- The reader reads the angle unit of a short-name file, or\n- a file that has an angle unit that the reader cannot resolve is refused by name. An angle is never read in a unit that the file does not state.\n\n## Done when\n\n- A STEP fixture that we made, with short names and a cone whose angle is in degrees, is in `testdata/models/`.\n- A test imports it. The cone has the correct angle (checked by a size that depends on the angle), or the import is refused by name.\n\nRefs #2919, #2927\n",
